        "mission_intent": "We need to stand up a focused collection effort on Russia's mechanisms for circumventing the G-7\u2013led price caps on crude oil and refined petroleum products. Specifically, we want to identify the non-Western shipping, insurance, and financial intermediaries Moscow is leveraging to divert seaborne oil exports, along with estimated volumes being sold above the cap thresholds. The collection plan should also cover Russia's continued LNG supply relationships with European buyers and any signals that Moscow is adjusting export volumes as a coercive tool against NATO cohesion on Ukraine. Coordinate with SIGINT and OSINT desks to map the network of shadow fleet vessels and flag-of-convenience registries involved. Reporting should feed into the next quarterly Russia Economic Leverage Assessment and should be structured to support sanctions enforcement recommendations. Please ensure the plan accounts for deconfliction with allied partner collection activities in the maritime domain. I'd like an initial collection strategy brief ready for review by the end of next week, with nominated priority intelligence requirements and proposed source taskings included.",
